@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: what crosses the workspace boundary UNCHANGED, what a clone re-materialises, and the four defects that turned out to be one
' covers: internal/workspace/mount.go
' covers: internal/workspace/deps.go
' covers: internal/proveohome/proveohome.go
' covers: internal/runlog/runlog.go
' The four instances this class was extracted from:
'   file PRESENCE ...... _spec/_plans/workspace-env-key.puml
'   MODE and OWNERSHIP . _spec/_plans/claudecode-autoupdater.puml (case B)
'   ARCHITECTURE ....... _spec/_plans/sbx-dep-tree-isolation.puml
'   WHICH TREE ......... _spec/_plans/connect-ide.puml
' The mode that dissolves it: _spec/internal/sbx/clone-workspace.puml
' The sibling boundaries: credential-boundary.puml, egress-boundary.puml,
'   runtime-user-boundary.puml (same directory)
' Notes here are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── THE CLASS, STATED ONCE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
' DIRECT MODE IMPORTS THE HOST'S FILESYSTEM SEMANTICS. A clone RE-MATERIALISES
' THEM. Every defect below is that one sentence meeting a different property of
' a file, and each was found separately, by a different route, and written up as
' its own plan before anyone noticed they rhymed.
'
'   PRESENCE       a `.env` beside the code exists inside the sandbox because it
'                  exists outside it. workspace-env-key.puml
'   MODE / OWNER   a `.claude/hooks/*.sh` the host can run is EACCES to a
'                  runtime uid that is not its owner.
'                  claudecode-autoupdater.puml, case B
'   ARCHITECTURE   a `node_modules` full of darwin-arm64 objects loads on the
'                  host and cannot load in the guest.
'                  sbx-dep-tree-isolation.puml
'   WHICH TREE     an editor attached to a clone edits a copy the operator will
'                  never see. connect-ide.puml
'
' A CLONE FIXES ALL FOUR AT ONCE, and not by intention: it carries TRACKED files
' only, git re-materialises them, and the result lands on an ext4 volume inside
' the VM owned by the runtime user with the one exec bit git records. So the
' gitignored `.env` never arrives, the hook arrives owned correctly, the foreign
' `node_modules` never arrives and the seed installs a native one, and there is
' no ambiguity about which tree an editor is editing — it is the clone, and the
' only question left is whether the operator was told.
'
' WHICH MAKES THE RESIDUAL PRECISE: every one of these is a DIRECT-MODE defect,
' clone mode is the sbx DEFAULT, and so each plan's real audience is the
' operator who turned the default off or whose workspace is not a repository.
' That population is worth measuring before any of them is built for.
'
' ── MEASURED, FROM INSIDE A LIVE SANDBOX ───────────────────────────────────
' Three readings that between them settle what the boundary does, all taken
' rather than reasoned:
'
'   THE MOUNT PERMITS EXECUTION. `host on /Users/… type virtiofs
'     (rw,nosuid,nodev,relatime)` — nosuid and nodev, NO noexec. So an
'     unexecutable file is a mode or ownership fault and never the mount's.
'   A CLONE IS NOT virtiofs AT ALL. The workspace showed as `/dev/vdj … ext4
'     (rw,relatime)` with files `-rwxr-xr-x 1 1000 1000`. That is why exec, uid
'     and architecture problems all vanish there together.
'   THE HOME MOUNT IS WIDER THAN ITS DECLARATION. `proveohome.Prepare` returns
'     ONE mount — the whole root, ReadOnly:false — while a def's `home.mounts`
'     list only decides what gets mkdir'd and scrubbed. Measured consequence:
'     `/proveo-home/logs/` lists EVERY prior run's transcript, owned by the
'     runtime user, and the directory is WRITABLE.
'
' THAT LAST ONE IS THE WORST OF THE FOUR and belongs to no single plan, which is
' partly why it went unowned: an agent can read and rewrite the transcript of
' its own run AND of every other run on the host. Integrity and confidentiality
' at once — a transcript carries the posture block, the detected providers, the
' secret NAMES that were stored and the workspace paths.
'
' ── THE RULE THAT GOVERNS EVERY REMEDY ─────────────────────────────────────
' NEVER REWRITE THE OPERATOR'S TREE WITHOUT AN EXPLICIT OPT-IN. In direct mode
' the workspace is their directory on their disk over virtiofs, so:
'   chmod'ing a hook to make it run          is not proveo's to do
'   installing native modules over theirs    breaks their host build
'   shredding a mounted `.env`               destroys their file
' This is not caution; it is the difference between fixing an agent and breaking
' a laptop. `PROVEO_DEPS=reinstall` is the shape a legitimate opt-in takes: it
' names the damage in the flag.
'
' ── THE THREE REMEDIES, AND WHAT EACH COSTS ────────────────────────────────
'   NARROW THE MOUNT      the only one that PREVENTS rather than detects. The
'                         home mount is the live case: honour the declared
'                         subpaths, or exclude `logs/`.
'   SHADOW A SUBPATH      a volume over `node_modules` (or `logs/`) leaves the
'                         host's untouched. Available on docker today via
'                         `workspace.DepCopy`; on sbx it waits on a Kit
'                         `volumes[]` field proveo does not model —
'                         sbx-dep-tree-isolation.puml owns that probe.
'   SAY SO EARLY          the seed already walks the workspace, so an
'                         unexecutable hook, a foreign object tree and a
'                         mounted key are all knowable BEFORE the agent starts.
'                         A posture line beats a failure an hour in.
'
' ── WHY THIS FILE EXISTS RATHER THAN A FIFTH PLAN ──────────────────────────
' The four instances were found on four different days, by four different
' routes, and each was written up as though it were the first. The cost of that
' is not duplication in the tree — it is that each one re-derived "clone mode
' already handles this; direct mode is the broken case" and none of them said it
' where the next reader would find it.
'
' So the next instance has somewhere to land. If a fifth property of a file
' turns out to cross unchanged — timestamps, extended attributes, case
' sensitivity, symlink targets — it is an entry above and not a new plan.
title Workspace boundary — direct mode imports the host's file semantics;\na clone re-materialises them

component "the operator's tree\ntheir disk, their modes, their arch" as HOST <<host>>

package "direct mode — virtiofs" as DIRECT <<host>> {
  component "PRESENCE\na mounted "".env""" as P1 <<error>>
  component "MODE / OWNER\nEACCES on a hook" as P2 <<error>>
  component "ARCHITECTURE\nforeign ""node_modules""" as P3 <<error>>
  component "WHICH TREE\nan editor on a copy" as P4 <<error>>
}
component "clone mode — ext4, git\ntracked files, uid 1000,\none exec bit" as CLONE <<app>>
database "**the home mount**\nthe whole root, rw —\nevery run's transcript" as HOME <<error>>
component "the agent" as AG <<app>>

HOST ARROW_ERROR DIRECT : crosses unchanged
HOST ARROW_MAIN CLONE : re-materialised
DIRECT ARROW_ERROR AG
CLONE ARROW_MAIN AG : all four dissolve at once
HOME ARROW_ERROR AG : readable AND writable,\nacross runs

note bottom of CLONE
  **It fixes all four by accident, not design.**
  Tracked files only, re-materialised by git onto
  ext4, owned by the runtime user, carrying the
  one exec bit git records. Every plan above is
  therefore a DIRECT-mode plan.
end note

note bottom of HOME
  **The worst of them, and it belonged to no
  plan.** ""Prepare"" mounts the root rw while
  a def declares subpaths, so an agent can rewrite
  its own transcript and every other run's —
  integrity and confidentiality together.
end note

note bottom of P3
  **The mount is not the culprit.** Measured:
  virtiofs here is ""nosuid,nodev"" and NOT
  ""noexec"". An unexecutable file is a mode or an
  owner, and a foreign object is an
  architecture — never the mount.
end note

note right of HOST
  **Never rewritten without an opt-in.** chmod'ing
  a hook, installing over their modules, wiping
  their "".env"" — each fixes an agent by breaking
  a laptop. ""PROVEO_DEPS=reinstall"" is what a
  legitimate opt-in looks like: it names the cost.
end note

legend bottom
  **What this file settles**
  ==
  **One sentence, four defects**: direct mode imports the host's filesystem semantics and
  a clone re-materialises them. Presence, mode, architecture and which-tree are that
  sentence meeting four properties of a file — found on four days, written up four times,
  each re-deriving the same conclusion where the next reader would not see it.
  --
  **So every one of those plans is a DIRECT-mode plan**, clone mode is the sbx default, and
  their real audience is whoever turned it off or is not in a repository. Measure that
  population before building for any of them.
  ==
  **The rule over every remedy**: never rewrite the operator's tree without an explicit
  opt-in. Narrowing the mount is the only remedy that PREVENTS; shadowing waits on a Kit
  field on sbx; saying so early is available today and unused.
  --
  **And the fifth instance has a home now.** Timestamps, xattrs, case sensitivity, symlink
  targets — if one of those crosses unchanged, it is a row here and not a new plan.
end legend
@enduml
